sections.body:
Confidential Information means any non-public information a Party shares with the other, in any form, that is marked confidential or that a reasonable person would treat as confidential. It does not include information that:
- is or becomes public through no fault of the receiving Party;
- the receiving Party already knew without a duty of confidentiality;
- the receiving Party develops independently; or
- a third party shares lawfully and without restriction.
